{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The epoxy fits my history of buying tape and vinyl cement because it offers another way to make durable repairs when those materials cannot hold.",
    "The adhesive-lined heat shrink and solder-seal connectors complement my earlier wire terminals by helping insulate and seal repaired connections. I would choose the adhesive-lined tubing over the basic kit for that added protection."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The nuts, washers and heavy battery lugs require specific matching sizes or wire gauges. Buying clamps and smaller wire terminals does not mean I currently need those particular fittings.",
    "Ten tubes of super glue exceed what I would choose for occasional repairs, while the magnets and electronic cleaner address tasks I have no current reason to tackle."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair purchases seem to have been treated as interest in almost any workshop supply, even when I have no clear use for it.",
    "My past Gorilla purchases and some large assortments seem to suggest more interest in bulk supplies than I actually have; the quantity still needs to make sense for the item."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "For wiring supplies, the kind of connection and compatible wire size matter more to me than simply being electrical repair equipment.",
    "I distinguish between useful assortments that cover several repair sizes and large quantities of one consumable or exact-size fitting that may sit unused."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my practical repair interests but sometimes missed the specific function, compatibility and quantity that would make a purchase useful now."
}"}
